[ganderse@adelphi.ua.oz.au.oz.au (Geoff Andersen) writes:]
[] Also do the items in the polypile change their curse/blessedness. eg if I
[] have a +5 longsword will it polymorph into, say, a +5 katana, or will it
[] be +0 or some random variation. Similarly, will an item remain cursed
[] under polymorph?

[water@wheaton.UUCP (Paul Waterman) writes:]
[] Polymorphing an object totally changes it.  The only thing which is
[] absolutely sure to remain the same is what general type of object it is
[] (i.e. scroll, potion, weapon, armor, etc.).  For instance, if you
[] polymorphed an uncursed longsword +1, you could end up with:
[] a blessed broadsword +3
[] a cursed dagger -2
[] an uncursed dart
[] Obviously, many other variations exist.

not quite ... to be sure, there are some (necessary) exceptions, however
if you polymorph an uncursed +1 long sword you'll end up with an uncursed
+1 <weapon>, similarly if polymorph a blessed +3 broadsword you'll end up
with a blessed +3 <weapon>, and so on (for armors, etc.).

in older versions of nethack the seemingly random nature of poly-piling
was an illusion created by the fact that the sequence of objects in the
pile was inverted.

